# Normalize line endings and encoding for text files, regardless of the
# committer's local `core.autocrlf` setting. Without this, a Windows
# checkout with autocrlf=true can commit CRLF-mangled UTF-8, which is how
# the mojibake in src/tools/*/handler.py (B5, ROADMAP-2026-08.md task 5.5)
# happened in the first place.

* text=auto working-tree-encoding=UTF-8

*.py text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
*.md text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
*.toml text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
*.json text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
*.jsonl text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
*.yml text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
*.yaml text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8

# Los datos, con eol=lf tambien en el arbol de trabajo. Sin fijarlo, `* text=auto`
# le da CRLF a un checkout de Windows y `scripts/build_programs_dataset.py`, que
# escribe LF, dejaria el fichero "modificado" en cada regeneracion aunque el dato
# fuera identico. La reproducibilidad que promete data/programs/README.md depende
# de esto.
*.csv text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
